# Regkasse — Cursor Rules (redirect + project index)

> **Single source of truth:** `AGENTS.md` at the repository root.
> Do **not** duplicate full development rules here — update `AGENTS.md` instead.
> This file is a short index so agents load the right context and stack before coding.

```yaml
project:
  name: Regkasse
  type: monorepo
  description: RKSV-compliant multi-tenant POS system (Austria)
  packages:
    - backend          # ASP.NET Core API, fiscal/TSE/RKSV
    - frontend         # Expo POS (cash-register)
    - frontend-admin   # Next.js admin panel (FA)
    - frontend-sites   # Next.js tenant storefronts
    - localization     # shared i18n tooling

context_files:
  always:
    - AGENTS.md
  medium_or_large_tasks:
    - REGKASSE_AI_ONBOARDING.md
    - docs/PROJECT_COMPREHENSIVE_DOCUMENTATION.md
  domain_as_needed:
    - ai/07_DO_NOT_TOUCH.md
    - ai/01_BACKEND_CONTRACT.md
    - ai/02_DATABASE_CONTRACT.md
    - ai/03_API_CONTRACT.md
    - ai/05_SECURITY_COMPLIANCE.md
    - ai/10_API_BOUNDARY_POLICY.md
  patterns_dataset:
    - ai/training/README.md
    - ai/training/regkasse-ai-dataset.json
    - ai/training/curated-patterns.json

coding_standards:  # details + versions in AGENTS.md § Repo Map
  backend:
    framework: ASP.NET Core 10
    orm: EF Core 10
    language: C#
  frontend_admin:
    framework: Next.js 16
    ui: Ant Design 6
    language: TypeScript
  mobile_pos:
    framework: Expo SDK 56
    language: TypeScript
  sites:
    framework: Next.js 16
    language: TypeScript

patterns:
  - Follow nearest existing package patterns; prefer incremental changes
  - Preserve backward compatibility unless explicitly told otherwise
  - Include tests for new features / high-risk changes
  - Do not invent APIs, roles, or fiscal flows — read contracts first

ai_assistance:
  prefer_existing_patterns: true
  respect_api_boundaries: true   # POS /api/pos/* vs Admin /api/admin/*
  respect_tenant_isolation: true # cross-tenant → HTTP 404, not 403
  read_recent_improvements: true # AGENTS.md § Recent Improvements (2026-07)
```

## Read order for AI agents
1. **`AGENTS.md`** — always-applied workspace rules (languages, multi-tenant, API boundaries, fiscal/backup guardrails, validation commands, recent DX/CI improvements)
2. **`REGKASSE_AI_ONBOARDING.md`** — project brief for medium/large tasks
3. **`docs/PROJECT_COMPREHENSIVE_DOCUMENTATION.md`** — broader system map when needed
4. **`ai/`** — domain contracts (`07_DO_NOT_TOUCH.md`, API/database/compliance, module docs)

## Quick reminders (non-exhaustive)
- **Languages:** POS UI German (de-DE); Admin UI i18n (de/en/tr); IDE explanations Turkish; code identifiers English.
- **API:** POS → `/api/pos/*` (+ Auth/Receipts); Admin → `/api/admin/*` — do not cross boundaries.
- **Tenancy:** Cross-tenant access → HTTP **404** (not 403). Never `IgnoreQueryFilters()` except Super Admin ops.
- **Stack (pinned):** .NET 10 / EF 10.0.10; FA Next.js 16 + Ant Design 6; POS Expo SDK 56 — see AGENTS.md for exact package versions.
- **FA Ant Design:** use `useNotify()` / `useAntdApp()` — never static `message` / `notification` / `Modal.confirm` from `antd`.
- **High-risk:** payments, TSE/RKSV chain, tenant isolation, FinanzOnline outbox, voucher ledger, backup/restore.
- **Recent DX (2026-07):** npm workspaces, path-filtered CI, OpenAPI→Orval + Husky verify, i18n hard gate — details in `AGENTS.md` § Recent Improvements.

**Last updated:** 2026-07-24 — enhanced project index; rules remain in AGENTS.md only.
